">As of Oct 12, the record here runs from 1951 to 2025 on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 34 of 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025, on the middle of the grids, April to May ran 151% of normal and November to December ran 56%. So far in 2026, February to March sits at 59% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 2007, with grid 18177 at 56%.</p>"}
